---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';

const toc = [
  { id: 'getting-started',  label: 'Getting started' },
  { id: 'dictate',          label: 'How to dictate' },
  { id: 'data',             label: 'Your data' },
  { id: 'troubleshooting',  label: 'Troubleshooting' },
  { id: 'contact',          label: 'Contact' },
];

const title = 'Support — Rekody';
const description = 'How to set up and use Rekody, plus answers to common questions.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <LegalPage
    eyebrow="Support"
    title="Help with Rekody."
    updated="July 10, 2026"
    summary="Speak, and Rekody types the words where your cursor is. Everything runs on your device."
    toc={toc}
  >
    <section id="getting-started">
      <h2>Getting started</h2>
      <p>
        Install Rekody, open it, and it walks you through setup: the permissions it needs to
        hear you and to type for you, and a one-time download of the on-device voice model.
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          Stay on a network for that first model download. After it finishes, dictation runs
          fully offline.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="dictate">
      <h2>How to dictate</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Start dictation. Rekody shows that it's listening.</li>
        <li>Speak. Your words appear live as you talk.</li>
        <li>Stop, or just pause — Rekody finishes on its own after a short silence.</li>
        <li>The text lands where your cursor is.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        You can keep working while you talk. Rekody follows along and places the finished
        text when you're done.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="data">
      <h2>Your data</h2>
      <p>
        Your audio never leaves your device. Your dictation history is stored locally, and
        you can delete any entry, or all of them, at any time. There are no accounts and no
        tracking. For the full picture, see the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="troubleshooting">
      <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
      <h3>The text didn't get typed</h3>
      <p>
        Rekody needs your system's permission to place text where your cursor is. Open your
        system settings, find Rekody, and make sure every permission it asked for during
        setup is still on.
      </p>
      <h3>Rekody won't record</h3>
      <p>
        Check that microphone access is on for Rekody in your system settings. The app shows
        a reminder if it's off.
      </p>
      <h3>Dictation is disabled in a password field</h3>
      <p>
        That's on purpose. Rekody turns itself off in password and other secure fields.
        Switch to a normal text field and it comes back.
      </p>
      <h3>The first dictation seems stuck</h3>
      <p>
        That's the one-time model download finishing. Keep Rekody open and stay on a
        network. Your words are captured while it loads, so nothing you say is lost.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:support@rekody.com">support@rekody.com</a>. Tell us your device
        and Rekody version and we'll help.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also join the
        <a href="https://discord.gg/J264YApCFN" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Rekody Discord</a>
        to ask questions, share what you're building, and tell us what to fix next.
      </p>
    </section>
  </LegalPage>
</Base>
